 # Raw News
 
+## Data Collection Status
+
+- Prepared deterministic raw news file was empty.
+- Project Google News RSS fetch failed in this sandbox with DNS resolution
+  errors, so web evidence was used for public market context.
+- Project quote and scanner fetches also failed on DNS/YFinance host resolution;
+  no broker, order, or credential data was used.
+- Because current deterministic price feeds were unavailable, this run must not
+  approve an order unless a setup has independent current price, entry, stop,
+  and risk evidence. That standard was not met.
+
 ## Macro Stories
 
+- [tier_B] Market close, 19 May 2026: Indian benchmarks erased intraday gains
+  and ended lower. Nifty 50 closed at 23,618.00, down 31.95 points, and Sensex
+  closed at 75,200.85, down 114 points. Rupee pressure and elevated crude were
+  cited as the main macro overhangs; IT was the leading positive sector while
+  private banks, financial services, and metals closed weak.
+  Source: https://upstox.com/news/market-news/stocks/sensex-nifty-50-erase-gains-end-lower-after-rupee-hits-new-record-low/article-193960/
+- [tier_B] Business Standard also described the same 19 May close as a lower
