-# 20 Bull
+# Bull Researcher
+
+## INFY
+
+1. INFY has the strongest tactical tape in the available universe. It closed up
+   4.76% near the 19 May high while the IT sector was the clear positive pocket.
+   Evidence: `01_news_raw.md`, `10_news.md`, `13_technical.md`.
+2. Weak rupee can support dollar-earning IT exporters, creating a plausible
+   sector-rotation setup even when the broader market is mixed. Evidence:
+   `10_news.md`.
+3. The stock has no identified governance/fundamental veto in this run.
+   Evidence: `12_fundamentals.md`.
+
+## TCS
+
+1. TCS participated in the IT rebound and remains a high-quality large-cap IT
+   franchise. Evidence: `01_news_raw.md`, `12_fundamentals.md`.
+2. Public quote data showed positive 19 May price action and substantial
+   liquidity, making it easy to monitor if the sector rally broadens. Evidence:
+   `02_setups_raw.md`.
+3. The same rupee/exporter tailwind that supports INFY can support TCS
+   sentiment. Evidence: `10_news.md`, `11_sentiment.md`.
+
+## SBIN
+
+1. SBIN closed up 1.00% even though private banks and financial services were
+   weak, giving it relative resilience within the tracked financial names.
+   Evidence: `01_news_raw.md`, `02_setups_raw.md`.
+2. Its public valuation data is not demanding versus large-cap peers, and no
+   fundamental veto was identified. Evidence: `12_fundamentals.md`.
+3. A public-sector-bank bid could persist if market participants rotate away
+   from private-bank weakness. Evidence: `10_news.md`, `13_technical.md`.
+
+## RELIANCE
+
+1. Reliance remains a fundamentally acceptable watchlist name from durable
+   memory, with Jio/Retail optionality and scale. Evidence:
+   `tradeloop/memory/stock_dossiers/RELIANCE.md`, `12_fundamentals.md`.
+2. The latest public print stayed above the prior invalidation level of 1311,
+   so the watchlist thesis is not fully dead. Evidence: `01_news_raw.md`,
+   `tradeloop/memory/carry_forward_context.md`.
+3. A future reclaim of 1365-1389 could create a cleaner technical repair setup.
+   Evidence: `13_technical.md`.
 
