    82	
    83	- symptom: a TradeLoop explanation sounds complete but overstates automation -> cause: the prep layer only seeds schema-first artifacts and some stages may still depend on later reasoning or fallback evidence -> fix: distinguish seeded placeholders from validated downstream outputs when describing the workflow [Task 1]
    84	- symptom: timezone-aware cron looks correct in a template but may not fire as expected on macOS -> cause: `CRON_TZ` support is fragile here -> fix: prefer the dispatcher pattern that checks `Asia/Kolkata` at runtime and verify the installed crontab, not just `tradeloop/scripts/crontab.txt` [Task 3]
    85	- symptom: Code Runner fails with `/usr/bin/env tradingbot ...` -> cause: `tradingbot` is a conda env name, not a binary, and the executor shape is wrong -> fix: run shell scripts under `bash`, keep the bash shebang, and use VS Code tasks or the logged wrapper [Task 4]
    86	- symptom: the user cannot follow a run because terminal scrollback hides earlier reasoning -> cause: terminal-only execution leaves no durable artifact for the full conversation/research transcript -> fix: launch through the log wrapper and inspect `tradeloop/reports/cycle_logs/latest.log` first [Task 4]
    87	- symptom: a huge adhoc log looks broken even though the workflow completed -> cause: Codex emitted long patch/diff transcripts and retries, and there may be recoverable network/MCP errors inside the log -> fix: check final artifacts plus `orders.json` / `fills.json` first, then inspect the log only for concrete failures [Task 5]
    88	- symptom: local technical-data fetch fails with `DNSError: Could not resolve host: guce.yahoo.com` -> cause: local Yahoo/yfinance resolution failed -> fix: call out the data-source fallback explicitly and separate "paper workflow finished" from "local data source was healthy" [Task 5]
